// Brother Teodor Ashe, mourning dove, the Unwriters (bible 3.3, character-bibles.md §4). The Quiet House (House_2).
// Voice: slow, complete sentences, gentle; never a raised voice. Asks permission before a hard sentence. Calls Wren
// "cartographer". Image: the faded in the present tense; he never says "was" of a bird.
// State he reads: Isolde, Aldermere's last day, the thread, the vigil, the library, the keystone.

title: QuietHouse_Teodor
---
<<if not has_flag("verdance.teodor.met")>>
    <<jump QuietHouse_Teodor_First>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.decided") and not has_flag("teodor.keystone_given") and not has_flag("teodor.refused")>>
    <<jump QuietHouse_Teodor_Keystone>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("teodor.keystone_given")>>
    Teodor: It is heavier than it looks. I told you. I carried it eleven years and it never got lighter. #still #line:0085c46
<<elseif has_flag("teodor.refused")>>
    Teodor: Sit, cartographer. The House does not close its door on a wrong answer. Only the stone stays. #still #line:04b879a
<<elseif has_flag("verdance.grove.vigil")>>
    Teodor: You sat with them. They are glad of it. Wenlow especially; Wenlow likes company. #line:0ad4246
<<else>>
    Teodor: The grove is lit tonight. It is always lit. Come when you are ready. There are no choices there. #line:04a96ab
<<endif>>
-> Why do the Cantors carry bells? #line:013d2f0
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Teodor: So that nobody is let go in silence. A bell is a kind of name. You will hear them. #line:0c9a9f5
-> What do you want from me? #line:06e339f
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Teodor: Nothing, yet. May I say a thing you will not like? You will want something from me. We will see. #line:09a8e70
-> Nothing today. #line:0d8bb8e
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Teodor: Then rest. The House is quiet for that reason, and no other. #line:029555f
===

title: QuietHouse_Teodor_First
---
Teodor: You are Isolde's. May I say a thing you will not like? #line:0d7fd22
-> Say it. #line:0eb86cb
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Teodor: She is a careful woman. She is careless with one thing. You are standing in it. #plant:5.2 #line:007fb66
-> Everyone says that first. #line:06bd070
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Teodor: Then everyone is careful. Sit. The reeds have been telling me about you for a week. #line:045e815
-> ... #line:0311a37
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Teodor: Good. The grove is quieter than that. You will do well there. #line:05d03fa
<<if has_flag("break.noticed.Verdance.OldRoad")>>
    Teodor: You crossed the iris gap without a wing. The old road remembers flyers. It will remember you. #line:06c99ac
<<endif>>
Teodor: I was a surveyor, once. I anchored eleven villages. I sit with them now, in the grove. #line:0dc23c6
Teodor: Aldermere holds its last day tomorrow. They asked us. Come, if you like. It is a kindness to be there. #line:0821dcb
<<flag verdance.teodor.met 1>>
===

title: QuietHouse_Teodor_Keystone
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.stopped")>>
    Teodor: You stopped Aldermere's last day. The Choir sang over me and I let it. #line:0251478
    Teodor: They are held now. Ask them whether they are glad. I have, every evening since. #line:0041558
    Teodor: The stone stays with me, cartographer. Not as a punishment. As a thing I am still sure of. #line:0207f89
    <<flag teodor.refused 1>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: You stood in the square to the end. May I ask you a thing, and hear an honest answer? #line:0d74f3a
Teodor: Why do I do this? Not the Unwriters. Me. Why do I let places go? #line:06d46ce
-> Because you were brave enough to. #line:01608c7
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Teodor: No. But you were close, and you were kind. I have been called brave. It was never true. #line:03fe572
    <<flag teodor.refused 1>>
-> Because they asked. And you made sure. #line:06fb014
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Teodor: Yes. That is why. They asked, and I made sure. #plant:5.1 #line:0a42618
    Teodor: The tenth, I was not sure. My mother asked, and I did it, and I have not been sure since. #line:00ce588
    Teodor: Take it. It is heavier than it looks. #line:0687df0
    <<flag teodor.keystone_given 1>>
    <<flag keystone.quiet_house 1>>
-> Because you grieve every one of them. #line:0782617
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Teodor: I do. But grief is not a reason. It is what a reason leaves. You were kind to say it. #line:03e5779
    <<flag teodor.refused 1>>
===
